{
  "runId": "ce-lite-vs-mattpocock-skills-msem7lj1-otxebv",
  "workflowName": "ce-lite-vs-mattpocock-skills",
  "script": "export const meta = {\n  name: \"ce-lite-vs-mattpocock-skills\",\n  description: \"WGS rubric + mattpocock/skills vs ce-lite goals and local skill inventory\",\n  phases: [\n    { title: \"Analyze\" },\n    { title: \"Synthesize\" },\n  ],\n};\n\nphase(\"Analyze\");\n\nconst catalog = `\nLOCAL SKILLS (subset of ~70+): ce-lite (+ companions reference/grilling/wayfinding/context-health/gather-judge),\nwriting-great-skills, grilling, grill-me, handoff, teach, to-questionnaire,\nharness-doctor, context-rot-forensics, poor-mans-distill, shard-security, graph-engineering,\nprompt-sharpen, no-ai-slop, find-skills, caveman-compress, full-output-enforcement,\nponytail, ponytail-review, and full mattpocock engineering set installed stock.\n\nMATTPOCOCK engineering catalog:\nUSER-INVOKED: ask-matt, grill-with-docs, triage, improve-codebase-architecture,\n  setup-matt-pocock-skills, to-spec, to-tickets, implement, wayfinder\nMODEL-INVOKED: prototype, diagnosing-bugs, research, tdd, domain-modeling,\n  codebase-design, code-review, resolving-merge-conflicts\nAlso upstream: design/ (product) set — out of scope unless fit is obvious.\n`;\n\nconst ceLiteGoals = `\nCE-LITE goals and mechanics:\n- Progressive depth: simple Q → direct; non-trivial → load ce-lite SKILL.md\n- Contract loop: grill → terms → plan → execute → verify → compound\n- Operator control; no process takeover (anti-GSD/BMAD)\n- Context health: handoff before rot; compaction fallback\n- gather-judge under judgment pressure\n- Multi-session wayfinding: plan decisions, not destinations; .scratch/wayfinding/\n- workflow tool for multi-agent fan-out; single-agent default\n- Compose existing skills (tdd, code-review, research…) rather than reimplement\n- Pi-native: lean-ctx, tiers, resumeFromRunId, saved workflows\n- Terse operator surface; hide protocol machinery\n\nLocal grill stack: ce-lite/grilling.md + grilling + grill-me + grill-with-docs (collision zone)\nLocal wayfinding: ce-lite/wayfinding.md vs matt wayfinder (collision zone)\nLocal handoff skill exists separately from ce-lite context-health\n`;\n\nconst wgsSummary = `\nwriting-great-skills (WGS) quality bar:\n- Description = WHAT + WHEN with trigger phrases AND negative triggers\n- Progressive disclosure: lean SKILL.md, details in linked files only when needed\n- Imperative steps matched to degrees of freedom / fragility\n- Composition over monoliths; prefer feedback loops\n- Anti-patterns: vague \"consider/should\", time estimates, windows-style walls,\n  essay-before-action, missing escape hatches, fighting sibling skills on same trigger\n- Glossary discipline for shared terms\n`;\n\nconst mattSkillNotes = `\nMatt skill behaviors (from installed SKILL.md bodies):\n- to-spec: deep requirements → frozen spec; user-invoked; pairs with grill\n- to-tickets: spec → vertical tickets; issue-tracker oriented\n- implement: pick ticket → TDD/code-review loop → done\n- wayfinder: multi-session roadmap / next-session steering\n- grill-with-docs: adversarial Qs grounded in docs\n- triage: classify request → route to right skill\n- ask-matt: meta Q about how to use the skill pack\n- improve-codebase-architecture: HTML architecture report heavyweight\n- prototype: spike before commit\n- diagnosing-bugs: systematic debug\n- research: codebase/external research\n- tdd: red-green-refactor discipline\n- domain-modeling: bounded contexts / model language\n- codebase-design: design patterns in repo\n- code-review: review checklist skill\n- resolving-merge-conflicts: conflict resolution\n- setup-matt-pocock-skills: install/configure the pack\n\nPhilosophy: small composable skills, operator chooses depth, disable-model-invocation on user-facing ones, no mega-framework takeover.\n`;\n\nconst localCollisionNotes = `\nKnown local forks/relatives:\n- grilling / grill-me: local adversarial clarification (may predate or diverge from grill-with-docs)\n- handoff: session continuity\n- teach: teaching mode\n- writing-great-skills: skill-authoring meta (WGS)\n- ce-lite: orchestration meta that should DELEGATE not duplicate matt skills\n- to-questionnaire: questionnaire extraction\n- harness-doctor / context-rot-forensics / poor-mans-distill: pi harness ops (matt has no equivalent)\n`;\n\nconst [criteria, inventory, fit, quality] = await parallel([\n  () =>\n    agent(\n      `Apply writing-great-skills as a scoring rubric for engineering agent skills in a pi harness + ce-lite stack.\n\n${wgsSummary}\n\n${ceLiteGoals}\n\nTask — return:\n1. Must-have quality bar (bullet list)\n2. 10 scored criteria (0-2 each) with what a \"2\" looks like\n3. Separate scoring axes: \"standalone WGS quality\" vs \"fits ce-lite\"\n4. Red flags → SKIP or REWRITE even if upstream popular\n\nTerse. Structured. No fluff.`,\n      { label: \"wgs-criteria\", tier: \"big\" }\n    ),\n  () =>\n    agent(\n      `Map mattpocock/skills against the local skill library.\n\n${catalog}\n${mattSkillNotes}\n${localCollisionNotes}\n${ceLiteGoals}\n\nFor EACH matt skill list:\n- Role in matt flow\n- Local status (stock present / duplicated by X)\n- ce-lite phase overlap (grill, terms, plan, execute, verify, compound, wayfind, handoff)\n- Collision risk (name the other skill)\n\nThen: pure gaps | local-only strengths | dangerous duplicates.\n\nSpecific filenames. Terse tables/bullets.`,\n      { label: \"inventory-map\", tier: \"medium\" }\n    ),\n  () =>\n    agent(\n      `Evaluate mattpocock/skills vs ce-lite goals.\n\n${ceLiteGoals}\n${mattSkillNotes}\n${localCollisionNotes}\n${catalog}\n\nAnswer:\n1. Right delegates per ce-lite phase (wiring table)\n2. Skills ce-lite must NOT auto-invoke (operator-only / collision)\n3. Philosophy align points\n4. Divergence points (issue trackers, CONTEXT.md/ADR, HTML arch reports, Claude-plugin defaults, disable-model-invocation)\n5. Pi-harness friction (workflow tool, tiers, lean-ctx, .scratch)\n\nPer matt skill: FIT | ADAPT | SKIP | REPLACE + one-line why.`,\n      { label: \"ce-lite-fit\", tier: \"big\" }\n    ),\n  () =>\n    agent(\n      `Audit mattpocock skill quality against WGS.\n\n${wgsSummary}\n${mattSkillNotes}\n\nce-lite is the local quality reference: progressive companions, terse SKILL.md, compose-don't-monolith.\n\nReturn:\n1. Overall grade A-F + evidence\n2. Best 3 WGS exemplars\n3. Weakest 3 + specific violations\n4. Systemic patterns (frontmatter, user vs model invoked, length, disclosure)\n5. Steal into ce-lite / local rewrites\n6. Do NOT copy\n\nTerse bullets.`,\n      { label: \"wgs-quality\", tier: \"medium\" }\n    ),\n]);\n\nphase(\"Synthesize\");\n\nconst synthesis = await agent(\n  `Staff-engineer synthesis for pi harness operator. Produce the final actionable plan.\n\n## Rubric\n${criteria || \"(missing coverage)\"}\n\n## Inventory\n${inventory || \"(missing coverage)\"}\n\n## Fit\n${fit || \"(missing coverage)\"}\n\n## Quality\n${quality || \"(missing coverage)\"}\n\nDeliver markdown:\n\n# mattpocock/skills × ce-lite — recommendations\n\n## Executive verdict\nOne short paragraph: keep/compose/prune stance.\n\n## Recommended wiring into ce-lite\nPhase → skill(s) + trigger rules. What ce-lite already owns vs should delegate.\n\n## Keep as-is\n## Adapt (fork or thin wrapper)\neach: change + why\n## Do not adopt / demote\neach: why\n## Gaps to author (WGS-quality)\neach: name, description draft (WHAT+WHEN), when, ce-lite plug-in point\n## Duplicate cleanup\nmerge/rename/negative-triggers\n## Priority order (next 5 actions)\nConcrete paths under skills/\n\nOpinionated. No URLs. No padding.`,\n  { label: \"synthesize\", tier: \"big\" }\n);\n\nreturn {\n  criteria: criteria || null,\n  inventory: inventory || null,\n  fit: fit || null,\n  quality: quality || null,\n  synthesis: synthesis || null,\n};",
  "sessionId": "019fcca7-14f0-705e-b5f0-bc36773ad4ac",
  "journal": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "runId": "ce-lite-vs-mattpocock-skills-msem7lj1-otxebv",
      "hash": "d8d2c929486bdd415a3f4155fbae00c26426039e4087c108b9e275d336a24903",
      "result": "# WGS × ce-lite scoring rubric (wgs-criteria / Analyze)\n\n## 1. Must-have quality bar (gate — fail any → don't score)\n- Correct invocation choice: `disable-model-invocation: true` unless the agent or another skill must reach it autonomously; if user-invoked and one of many, covered by a router skill.\n- Description starts on its leading word, does WHAT + WHEN, one trigger per branch, negative triggers where siblings compete (\"not for X — use Y\").\n- SKILL.md is lean: steps are primary tier; heavy protocol disclosed behind condition-worded context pointers (\"Read X when…\"), not inline.\n- Every step ends on a checkable completion criterion; flat reference carries an exhaustiveness bar (\"every rule applied\").\n- Prompts the positive; prohibitions only as hard guardrails, each paired with the target behavior.\n- No no-op lines (each line changes behavior vs the model default), no duplicated meaning anywhere in the skill system — one source of truth per meaning.\n- Escape hatches: stated defaults instead of questions, \"if in doubt →\" routes, handoff path for long runs.\n- Operator-control preserved: never asks the operator to name skills, tools, or stage transitions.\n\n## 2. Scored criteria (0–2 each, 20 total)\n\n**Axis A — standalone WGS quality (6 criteria, /12)**\n1. **Invocation discipline.** 2: description pays context load only because autonomous reach is required; user-invoked skills are lean by design and router-covered.\n2. **Trigger precision.** 2: leading word the operator actually says; branches are genuinely distinct (no synonym restating); negative triggers disambiguate the grilling/wayfinding/handoff collision zones.\n3. **Information hierarchy.** 2: progressive disclosure done right — inline what every branch needs, disclose what only some branches reach; pointers worded by firing condition.\n4. **Completion criteria & legwork.** 2: criteria checkable AND exhaustive; demands force legwork (\"every modified model accounted for\"), not \"produce a change list\".\n5. **Leading words & positive steering.** 2: pretrained words anchor regions with priors recruited free; zero no-ops; zero elephants; guardrails paired with positive targets.\n6. **SSOT, co-location, pruning.** 2: each meaning lives once; definition+rules+caveats under one heading; no sediment, no sprawl — file length matches live, unique content.\n\n**Axis B — fits ce-lite (4 criteria, /8)**\n7. **Contract-loop fit.** 2: slots cleanly into one phase (grill/terms/plan/execute/verify/compound) or composes as a callable; no competing loop, no stage-name exposure to the operator.\n8. **Composition over reimplementation.** 2: points at tdd/code-review/research/domain-modeling rather than restating them; explicitly resolves its collision with ce-lite internals (grilling.md, wayfinding.md, context-health.md).\n9. **Progressive depth & context health.** 2: zero standing load until invoked; honors handoff triggers and compacts via `.scratch/` artifacts; returns worker-result-contract evidence, transcripts stay out of chat.\n10. **Pi-native mechanics.** 2: uses `workflow` tiers (small/medium/big), `resumeFromRunId`, lean-ctx, saved workflows; single-agent default with fan-out justified by action- vs context-bound diagnose.\n\nScore bands: 18–20 adopt · 14–17 adopt w/ named fixes · 10–13 REWRITE · <10 SKIP. Axes independent: high-A/low-B stays standalone, never wired into ce-lite; low-A/high-B gets body rewritten, routing kept.\n\n## 3. Red flags → SKIP/REWRITE even if upstream popular\n- Second generalist trigger surface (\"use for any request\") — only ce-lite may own that branch; two orchestrators fight every turn.\n- Process takeover: mandatory ceremonies, gated stage checklists, asking a non-developer operator to pick skills/tools (GSD/BMAD pattern).\n- Third grilling clone or second wayfinding protocol — the meaning exists twice already (ce-lite/grilling.md + /grilling+grill-me+grill-with-docs; ce-lite/wayfinding.md + matt wayfinder); REWRITE to point at the SSOT, don't add a third home.\n- Handoff logic that duplicates context-health.md's trigger protocol instead of extending it (standalone /handoff is user-invoked artifact-writing; anything model-invoked auto-firing handoffs collides).\n- Vague imperatives (\"consider\", \"should\", \"be thorough\"), time estimates, windows-style walls, essay-before-first-action.\n- Negation-steering (\"never X, don't Y\") without positive targets.\n- Monolith grill→plan→execute→verify in one file — REWRITE as composition of existing skills.\n- Model-invoked with no distinct leading word — context load paid for nothing.\n- Cross-harness port artifacts: hard-coded model names, nonexistent tools/MCP calls, Claude-isms.\n- Transcript-dumping workers; no terse evidence JSON.\n- Any skill that doesn't hide protocol machinery from the operator.\n\nCollision-zone verdict for the local stack: keep matt `wayfinder` (user-invoked, tracker-backed) and make ce-lite/wayfinding.md a pointer + local-markdown delta; collapse ce-lite/grilling.md and /grilling to one source with the other as a thin reference; leave /handoff user-invoked as-is — no model-side collision exists.",
      "storeDelta": {}
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "runId": "ce-lite-vs-mattpocock-skills-msem7lj1-otxebv",
      "hash": "f00a42b4a7875d5ab4d825ba80b6c9cf9b2d4c16dcba329e02cfa999c1e2bc72",
      "result": "1. **Overall Grade: B+**\n   * **Evidence**:\n     * High predictability and strong focus on actionable feedback loops (e.g., `diagnosing-bugs`' \"red-capable\" loop constraint).\n     * Strong vocabulary integration with powerful pretrained leading words (\"frontier\", \"fog of war\", \"seam\", \"tracer-bullet\", \"blast radius\").\n     * Systemic violation of `disable-model-invocation: true` across the entire pack. Every skill disables model invocation but keeps a bloated description containing rich machine-facing trigger lists, violating WGS glossary rules for user-invoked skills (which require stripped, single-line summaries to eliminate context load).\n     * Inconsistent progressive disclosure: some skills use it beautifully, while others like `wayfinder` sprawl.\n\n2. **Best 3 WGS Exemplars**\n   * **`diagnosing-bugs/SKILL.md`**: Excellent predictability. Forces a \"red-capable\" feedback loop before any code execution. Uses \"tight\" and \"red-capable\" as leading words. Clear escape hatch if a loop cannot be built.\n   * **`code-review/SKILL.md`**: Great co-location and composition. Separates Standards vs. Spec into parallel sub-agents so they do not pollute contexts, and co-locates Fowler code smells as flat, readable reference.\n   * **`tdd/SKILL.md`**: Model progressive disclosure. Outsources deep implementation examples and mocking rules to `tests.md` and `mocking.md`, keeping the root SKILL.md focused solely on the red-green loop.\n\n3. **Weakest 3 + Specific Violations**\n   * **`implement/SKILL.md`**: Extreme brevity failure. A 5-line skeleton with no process, checkable steps, or completion criteria, offloading all execution burden to other sub-skills.\n   * **`wayfinder/SKILL.md`**: Violates WGS \"Sprawl\" and progressive disclosure guidelines. Piles extensive templates, ticket types, and state transitions into a 300-line monolith instead of utilizing companion reference files.\n   * **`to-spec/SKILL.md`**: Relies on weak, advisory \"should\" language anti-patterns (\"Existing seams should be preferred\", \"propose them at the highest point you can\") instead of imperative instructions or exhaustive completion criteria.\n\n4. **Systemic Patterns**\n   * **Frontmatter mismatch**: Every skill sets `disable-model-invocation: true` yet includes complex, machine-triggering descriptions. The trigger-phrase lists are redundant sediment.\n   * **Bifurcated disclosure**: Split between high-discipline files that outsource references to Markdown sub-files (`tdd`, `codebase-design`) and monolithic files that collect everything in-place (`wayfinder`, `diagnosing-bugs`).\n   * **Composition focus**: High systemic compliance with composition over monoliths; the skills are mapped as a single interconnected pipeline via `ask-matt`.\n\n5. **Steal into ce-lite / Local Rewrites**\n   * **Red-capable loops**: Integrate `diagnosing-bugs`' \"red-capable\" verification loop constraint into `ce-lite`'s verification and execution phases to prevent premature completion.\n   * **Expand-contract refactoring**: Port `to-tickets`' \"expand-contract\" blueprint for wide refactors into the planning phase of `ce-lite` to sequence large-scale codebase edits safely.\n   * **Standards vs. Spec duality**: Use parallel sub-agents during `ce-lite`'s worker verify phase to assess deliverables against raw spec requirements and design patterns independently.\n\n6. **Do NOT copy**\n   * This audit captures core conceptual lessons and structural patterns without copying any file bodies.",
      "storeDelta": {}
    },
