      "result": "### Matt Skills Map\n\n| Skill | Role in Matt Flow | Local Status | ce-lite Overlap | Collision Risk & Target |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `ask-matt` | Meta-router and directory for engineering skills. | Present: `skills/ask-matt/SKILL.md` | **Route** (Initial dispatch) | Low; meta-directory utility. |\n| `grill-with-docs` | Adversarial interview to sharpen requirements; outputs ADRs/glossary. | Present: `skills/grill-with-docs/SKILL.md` | **Grill** & **Compound** | High; collides with `grilling` and `ce-lite/grilling.md`. |\n| `triage` | State-machine issue/PR classifier and brief builder. | Present: `skills/triage/SKILL.md` | **Grill** & **Terms** | Low; pre-development tracker filter. |\n| `improve-codebase-architecture` | Code scan for deep-module boundaries; generates HTML report. | Present: `skills/improve-codebase-architecture/SKILL.md` | **Plan** & **Grill** | None; advanced decoupled architecture tool. |\n| `setup-matt-pocock-skills` | Repo setup for labels, trackers, and document templates. | Present: `skills/setup-matt-pocock-skills/SKILL.md` | None (Setup phase) | None. |\n| `to-spec` | Compiles chat/conversation into formal specs. | Present: `skills/to-spec/SKILL.md` | **Terms** (Specs/CONTRACT.md) | Low; merges into contract terms. |\n| `to-tickets` | Slices specs into dependency-linked issue-tracker tickets. | Present: `skills/to-tickets/SKILL.md` | **Plan** & **Wayfind** | Low; outputs to issue trackers. |\n| `implement` | Direct worker implementing tickets via TDD and review. | Present: `skills/implement/SKILL.md` | **Execute** & **Verify** | High; mapped to `ce-lite`'s primary execution subagent. |\n| `wayfinder` | Multi-session task/decision planner tracking via issues. | Present: `skills/wayfinder/SKILL.md` | **Wayfind** (Multi-session routing) | High; collides with `ce-lite/wayfinding.md` (local file maps). |\n| `prototype` | Builds throwaway code/UI spikes to answer design questions. | Present: `skills/prototype/SKILL.md` | **Plan** & **Execute** | Low; leveraged for prototype tickets. |\n| `diagnosing-bugs` | Structured hypothesis-driven bug and regression debugger. | Present: `skills/diagnosing-bugs/SKILL.md` | **Diagnose** & **Execute** | Low; used as the default diagnostic shelf tool. |\n| `research` | Deep-dives external documentation and resources. | Present: `skills/research/SKILL.md` | **Diagnose** & **Plan** | Low; called for external knowledge tasks. |\n| `tdd` | Code changes driven by Red-Green-Refactor testing. | Present: `skills/tdd/SKILL.md` | **Execute** & **Verify** | Low; called for test-first implementation. |\n| `domain-modeling` | Formulates bounded context ubiquitous vocabulary. | Present: `skills/domain-modeling/SKILL.md` | **Grill** & **Compound** | Low; run during grilling. |\n| `codebase-design` | Architectural vocabulary for deep decoupled modules. | Present: `skills/codebase-design/SKILL.md` | **Plan** | None. |\n| `code-review` | Compares diffs against repo Standards and Spec. | Present: `skills/code-review/SKILL.md` | **Verify** | Low; triggered as subagent verification. |\n| `resolving-merge-conflicts` | Interactive Git conflict resolution runner. | Present: `skills/resolving-merge-conflicts/SKILL.md` | **Execute** | None. |\n\n---\n\n### Pure Gaps\n*   **Issue Tracker State Machines**: The local library lacks out-of-the-box automation for native issue-tracker lifecycles (triage flow, native GitHub/GitLab label and ticket linking) without using `triage` or `setup-matt-pocock-skills`.\n*   **Standardized ADRs/Glossary Output**: Local code has no built-in standard formats for Architecture Decision Records (`ADR-FORMAT.md`) and Ubiquitous Languages (`CONTEXT-FORMAT.md`) without calling Matt's modeling set.\n\n---\n\n### Local-Only Strengths\n*   **Operational Telemetry & Health**: `harness-doctor/SKILL.md` (preflight shim checks, provider configuration) and `context-rot-forensics/SKILL.md` (statistical analysis of context knee collapse and real-time rot warning) have no Matt equivalents.\n*   **Token Optimization**: `caveman-compress/SKILL.md` shrinks memory files (like CLAUDE.md) down to high-density caveman-speak. `poor-mans-distill/SKILL.md` harvests successful session traces to distill non-fine-tuned few-shot specialists.\n*   **Context/Budget Containment**: `ce-lite/SKILL.md` explicitly routes complex tasks to multi-agent subagent budgets (via `workflow` fanning out under `graph-engineering/SKILL.md`) to isolate context footprints.\n*   **YAGNI Enforcement**: `ponytail/SKILL.md` and `ponytail-review/SKILL.md` strictly prevent over-engineering, pruning abstractions to focus on stdlib-first minimal implementations.\n*   **Non-Developer Bridging**: `to-questionnaire/SKILL.md` extracts unresolvable gaps into async survey documents for stakeholders.\n\n---\n\n### Dangerous Duplicates\n*   **Wayfinding Clash**: `skills/wayfinder/SKILL.md` vs. `ce-lite/wayfinding.md`. Matt's wayfinder pushes planning, blocking edges, and decision issues to the remote tracker (cluttering repositories). `ce-lite` uses local, lightweight `.scratch/wayfinder/MAP.md` files to save tokens, stay offline, and avoid repo pollution.\n*   **Handoff Overlap**: `skills/handoff/SKILL.md` vs. `ce-lite/context-health.md`. The former is manually run and dumps files to the OS temp directory; the latter is trigger-driven, tracks cumulative turn/rot metrics, and creates `.scratch/HANDOFF.md` alongside a resume-ready workflow `runId`.\n*   **Grilling Collisions**: `skills/grill-with-docs/SKILL.md` vs. `ce-lite/grilling.md` / `skills/grilling/` / `skills/grill-me/`. Matt's variant is document-generation heavy (ADRs, glossary focus). `ce-lite`'s grilling flow focuses strictly on blocking/fog decisions to produce checkable contract terms, delegating domain modeling only when terms are resolved.",
